WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/components/layout/LayoutBreadcrumbs.tsx — a thin wrapper that composes two SYNCHRONOUS derivations:
    • useBreadcrumbOverrides()  (components/layout/BreadcrumbOverridesContext.tsx) — the per-route-pattern label
                                 override map a page registers once its entity loads (e.g. "Drive #4421" →
                                 "Trip to office").
    • useBreadcrumbs(overrides) (hooks/useBreadcrumbs.ts) — matches location.pathname against the registered
                                 route patterns (lib/routeMeta.ts = ROUTE_META derived from routeRegistry.ts +
                                 PARENT_OVERRIDES) and walks `meta.parent` upward, unshifting each crumb so the
                                 trail reads [topmost ancestor … matched leaf]. Label precedence is
                                 override > t(i18nKey, defaultLabel); `{{param}}` is filled in the label and
                                 `:param` in the href; the matched (current) crumb gets NO href; the walk is
                                 cycle-guarded; an unmatched path yields [].
  It renders <Breadcrumbs items=… /> (components/layout/Breadcrumbs.tsx), which:
    • self-suppresses when items.length <= 1 (top-level pages render an empty slot — the surrounding layout row
      keeps the "Ctrl+K to jump" hint);
    • otherwise renders nav[aria-label=t('a11y.breadcrumb','Breadcrumb')] → a leading Home icon link to '/'
      (aria-label t('a11y.breadcrumbHome','Dashboard')) → chevron-separated crumbs; ancestors are PrefetchLinks
      (text-muted hover:text-secondary), the leaf is plain text (text-secondary font-medium); middle crumbs
      collapse to an ellipsis on a narrow width (hidden sm:inline + sm:hidden …); the row scrolls horizontally
      (overflow-x-auto scrollbar-none).
  Data sources (prompt): useBreadcrumbOverrides, useBreadcrumbs. Charts/maps used: none. i18n keys extracted:
  none literal in LayoutBreadcrumbs.tsx itself; the rendered Breadcrumbs resolves a11y.breadcrumb +
  a11y.breadcrumbHome and the route labels (routes.*). There are NO async / loading / error / stale / offline
  branches in the web source — the two hooks are a useMemo + a React context read; the surface's only real
  branches are the matched-route parent walk and the <=1 self-suppression. The P4 leaf contract
  (loading / error + a live/stale/offline freshness axis) is layered on top, modelled honestly as the
  navigation host's lifecycle + the freshness of the asynchronously-enriched override labels.

